// RUN: strip-comments.sh %s | filecheck %s
// RUN: strip-comments.sh %s | filecheck %s --strict-whitespace --check-prefix=STRICT
// RUN: strip-comments.sh %s | filecheck %s --strict-whitespace --match-full-lines --check-prefix=FULL

// Regression test for whitespace handling around the check string.
//
// Upstream FileCheck strips leading and trailing whitespace from the check
// string in every mode, except when both --strict-whitespace and
// --match-full-lines are given, in which case whitespace is part of the
// pattern. A space (or several) between the prefix and the pattern must
// therefore not require the input line to start with whitespace.
//
// Every check uses a unique token with its own input line, so no check
// can match another case's line. In full-line strict mode the pattern is
// anchored to the whole line, so those lines carry the leading whitespace
// the pattern requires.

// -- leading whitespace after the colon is ignored ---------------------

// no space after the colon
// CHECK:A
// STRICT:A
// FULL:A
A

// one space
// CHECK: B
// STRICT: B
B
// FULL: C
 C

// two spaces
// CHECK:  D
// STRICT:  D
D
// FULL:  E
  E

// three spaces
// CHECK:   F
// STRICT:   F
F
// FULL:   G
   G

// -- trailing whitespace in the pattern is ignored ---------------------

// the lines below carry an intentional trailing space
// trailing spaces are stripped from the pattern
// CHECK:H 
// STRICT:H 
// ... except in full-line strict mode, where they are part of the pattern
// FULL:H 
H 
